{"entryId":"3184","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:3184:1","sourceSha256":"9802e9b9bf6cbd6e398c25b07f81badbdd914e5871ed731fe9d6980606a2b93f","englishSha256":"a996c90c20d187137d71495edeebc0a8f4fc575e024ca6ff4ebfcfbf6622f8d6","citations":[{"id":"3184:1:link-001","he":[0,19],"en":[0,31],"target":{"url":"https://www.daat.ac.il/daat/vl/yohasin-zakut/yohasin-zakut09.pdf#page=39"},"reference":"Sefer Yuhasin, Treatise II, London 1857, p. 183","assessment":"The London Yuhasin heads with Rava and preserves a bracketed Rabbah variant. It explicitly describes a statement to Rav Ashi.","evidence":[{"reference":"Sefer Yuhasin, Treatise II, London 1857, p. 183","target":{"url":"https://www.daat.ac.il/daat/vl/yohasin-zakut/yohasin-zakut09.pdf#page=39"},"witness":"Sefer Yuhasin, Treatise II, London 1857, p. 183"},{"reference":"Sotah 26b:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sotah_26b.10"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3184:1:link-002","he":[25,42],"en":[36,45],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Eruvin_3a.20"},"reference":"Eruvin 3a:20","assessment":"Eruvin names Rava of Parzika twice, with no address to Rav Ashi in those two passages.","evidence":[{"reference":"Eruvin 3a:20","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Eruvin_3a.20"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Eruvin 3a:25","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Eruvin_3a.25"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3184:1:link-003","he":[43,58],"en":[47,56],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sotah_26b.10"},"reference":"Sotah 26b:10","assessment":"Rava of Parzakia explicitly addresses Rav Ashi.","evidence":[{"reference":"Sotah 26b:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sotah_26b.10"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3184:1:link-004","he":[59,72],"en":[58,88],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Zevachim_10b.24"},"reference":"Zevachim 10b:24","assessment":"The named dialogue is not present on checked 9b. On 10b, the same tractate has the exact exchange with both names. Link to the evidenced dialogue with a qualified locator correction.","evidence":[{"reference":"Zevachim 10b:24","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Zevachim_10b.24"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Zevachim 9b:21","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Zevachim_9b.21"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3184:1:link-005","he":[73,85],"en":[90,104],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Kamma_36a.2"},"reference":"Bava Kamma 36a:2","assessment":"Rava of Parzika explicitly addresses Rav Ashi.","evidence":[{"reference":"Bava Kamma 36a:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Kamma_36a.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3184:1:link-006","he":[106,125],"en":[139,158],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Pesachim_76b.10"},"reference":"Pesachim 76b:10","assessment":"Pesahim names Rava of Parzika issuing a ruling, followed by a stricter ruling from Mar bar Rav Ashi. It does not record dialogue with Rav Ashi there.","evidence":[{"reference":"Pesachim 76b:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Pesachim_76b.10"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3184:1:link-007","he":[127,166],"en":[159,212],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Nazir_38b.8"},"reference":"Nazir 38b:8","assessment":"The checked Nazir text names Ravina of Parzikia addressing Rav Ashi. Heilprin’s proposed Rava expansion and its asserted edition support require printed collation.","evidence":[{"reference":"Nazir 38b:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Nazir_38b.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3184:1:link-008","he":[215,274],"en":[389,395],"target":{"url":"https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/יבמות_נט_ב"},"reference":"Yevamot 59b, Wikisource Hebrew transcription","assessment":"The actual locus is Yevamot 59b. Another Heilprin notice gives 59b explicitly. The checked Wikisource text reads Parkin and the vocalized Davidson text reads Parzakia.","evidence":[{"reference":"Yevamot 59b, Wikisource Hebrew transcription","target":{"url":"https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/יבמות_נט_ב"},"witness":"Yevamot 59b, Wikisource Hebrew transcription"},{"reference":"Yevamot 59b:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yevamot_59b.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Sotah 26b:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sotah_26b.10"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3184:1:link-009","he":[215,274],"en":[516,543],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yevamot_59b.8"},"reference":"Yevamot 59b:8","assessment":"The actual locus is Yevamot 59b. Another Heilprin notice gives 59b explicitly. The checked Wikisource text reads Parkin and the vocalized Davidson text reads Parzakia.","evidence":[{"reference":"Yevamot 59b:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yevamot_59b.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Yevamot 59b, Wikisource Hebrew transcription","target":{"url":"https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/יבמות_נט_ב"},"witness":"Yevamot 59b, Wikisource Hebrew transcription"},{"reference":"Sotah 26b:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sotah_26b.10"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3184:1:link-010","he":[276,311],"en":[544,599],"target":{"entry":319,"paragraph":1},"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Tanaim and Amoraim 319:1","assessment":"Entry 319 uses Parzila and explicitly points back to Rabbah of Parzika. This is a genuine pointer and an attributed conjecture.","evidence":[{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 319:1","target":{"entry":319,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"}]},{"id":"3184:1:link-011","he":[313,345],"en":[600,645],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Ketubot_10a.13"},"reference":"Ketubot 10a:13","assessment":"The exact locus Ketubot gives Huna Mar son of Rava of Parzakia addressing Rav Ashi. The separate Huna entry cites the same clause.","evidence":[{"reference":"Ketubot 10a:13","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Ketubot_10a.13"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 985:1","target":{"entry":985,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7,9,10],"holds":[{"raw":"רבא מפרזיקא לרב אשי וכן בפסחים","reason":"Sotah and Bava Kamma have a direct address. The bounded Eruvin loci give statements without an addressee, and Pesahim gives a ruling followed by one from Mar bar Rav Ashi. The catalogue’s grouping is preserved as a report.","evidence":[{"reference":"Eruvin 3a:20","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Eruvin_3a.20"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Eruvin 3a:25","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Eruvin_3a.25"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Pesachim 76b:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Pesachim_76b.10"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Sotah 26b:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sotah_26b.10"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"raw":"וכ\"מ בש\"ס חדשים נוסחא אחרת רבא מפרזקי","reason":"The printed Yuhasin witness attests both Rava and Rabbah for this heading, but the checked Nazir reads Ravina. The precise new-Shas edition alleged to read Rava in Nazir remains unidentified.","evidence":[{"reference":"Nazir 38b:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Nazir_38b.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Sefer Yuhasin, Treatise II, London 1857, p. 183","target":{"url":"https://www.daat.ac.il/daat/vl/yohasin-zakut/yohasin-zakut09.pdf#page=39"},"witness":"Sefer Yuhasin, Treatise II, London 1857, p. 183"}]},{"raw":"ונראה כי אחד הוא","reason":"The Aha entry points back here with yet another place spelling. Current witnesses do not adjudicate Heilprin’s conjecture of identity.","evidence":[{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 319:1","target":{"entry":319,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"},{"reference":"Sotah 26b:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sotah_26b.10"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"notes":[{"text":"The checked Zevahim exchange occurs at 10b. Yevamot 59b has Parkin in the checked Wikisource text and Parzakia in Davidson. The newer Nazir edition, the proposed Aha identification and the extent of the Ashi grouping remain qualified.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Zevachim 10b:24","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Zevachim_10b.24"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Zevachim 9b:21","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Zevachim_9b.21"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Yevamot 59b, Wikisource Hebrew transcription","target":{"url":"https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/יבמות_נט_ב"},"witness":"Yevamot 59b, Wikisource Hebrew transcription"},{"reference":"Yevamot 59b:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yevamot_59b.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Sotah 26b:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sotah_26b.10"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"entryEvidence":[]}
